# Repo-root ignores. Each package under packages/* has its own .gitignore for its runtime files
# (config.json, data/, logs/, state/, etc.).

# .claude is local-only EXCEPT checked-in slash commands (.claude/commands/).
# Use .claude/* (not .claude/) so the negation can re-include a subdirectory.
.claude/*
!.claude/commands/

# Ignore vs code workspace files, which are local-only.
.vscode/
*.code-workspace

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything below is repo-wide. gitignore rules never apply upward, so a package's .gitignore does
# nothing for the root -- these were all uncovered at the root until now.

# Python bytecode and build artifacts. tools/ and scripts/ hold real runnable code at the root.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# Virtualenvs. scripts/dev-install.{ps1,sh} is the documented install path and the docs tell you to
# make one, so an accidentally committed .venv is a realistic (and enormous) mistake.
.venv/
venv/

# Tool caches. ruff and pytest each write their own .gitignore inside these, which is what kept them
# invisible before -- declare them so that stays true regardless of tool version or behavior.
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Scratch work. Every package's CLAUDE.md states "scratch work goes in a gitignored .tmp/"; all seven
# packages honored that and the root did not, so following the rule here used to commit the file.
.tmp/

# Secrets live in the OS keyring only -- never a file in the tree.
.env
.env.*

# Local-only authoring artifacts (graphify is opt-in tooling, never a runtime dependency).
graphify-out/

# Runtime output, should anything ever write at the root rather than under ~/.cherrypick. `data/` at
# the ROOT is not suite data -- no package writes there; it is the local agent-memory MCP store,
# which picks the working directory when it is run from here. Suite data lives under ~/.cherrypick.
data/
logs/
state/
dashboard.html
*.bak

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
